## Metadata
- Author: [[Ziwei Xu, Sanjay Jain]]
- Full Title: Hallucination is Inevitable- An Innate Limitation of Large Language Models
- Category: #articles
- Summary:: Hallucination is a well-known issue in large language models (LLMs), with efforts made to minimize it empirically. However, this paper argues that complete elimination of hallucination in LLMs is impossible. By defining a formal world where hallucination is inconsistencies between LLMs and ground truth functions, the study concludes that LLMs cannot learn all computable functions and will always exhibit hallucinations. The research suggests that since the formal world mirrors the real world, hallucinations are inevitable in real-world LLMs. Additionally, the study identifies tasks prone to hallucination and discusses existing mitigators and implications for the safe use of LLMs.
- URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.11817

